    \field{sortinit}{C}
    \field{sortinithash}{C}
    \field{abstract}{%
    Technical professionals are a key factor for IT product development. In an
  IT company, it is common for an employee to hold multiple skills.
  Multi-skilled staff increases the difficulty of project portfolio scheduling
  and staff assignment. This paper helps R&D managers cope with the problem by
  proposing a multi-objective optimization model of project portfolio
  scheduling and multi-skilled staff assignment. The model considers three
  objectives with strong practicality, i.e., staff skill enhancement,
  development cycle time, and product quality, and incorporates skill
  cultivation through a learning curve. We then propose an improved
  multi-objective Pareto ant colony optimization algorithm combining genetic
  operators to find an approximate Pareto solution set. Personalized decision
  rules with strong practicability are also discussed for selecting an
  appropriate solution. A case study in a leading electrical device company in
  China demonstrates the utility of the proposed model and algorithm.%
    }
