    \field{abstract}{%
    Traditional production scheduling and control are increasingly inadequate
  in light of the rapid evolution of manufacturing technology, the growing
  impact of unforeseen disruptions, and the generally increasing complexity of
  production. A framework for future-proof production scheduling and control is
  introduced to close this gap, providing a comprehensive overview of future
  requirements and the necessary technologies and approaches. Robust decision
  criteria are derived, explained and filled with major recent advances in
  production scheduling and control, digital twins, artificial intelligence,
  and knowledge formalisation. Emerging trends are discussed, and an outlook
  for future research and decision-making is derived.%
    }
